# Agent ledger and resume protocol -- {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Purpose: no progress is lost to a usage limit, an account switch, or a
dead session, and work resumes exactly where it stopped. Part of the
optional speed mode (`SPEED-MODE.md`). Update the roster at every launch
and every finish.

**This file never contains credentials.** Not a password, a key, or a
token value -- not even a short-lived one. If a scoped token is in use,
write only that one exists, what it is scoped to, and when it must be
revoked.

## How work is kept safe (rules for every builder agent)

1. Own git worktree, own feature branch.
2. A `wip: <what>` commit after every logical step, then
   `git push -u origin <its own branch>`. Own branch only: never the
   default branch, never a merge, never a force-push.
3. The branch history is the progress record; the final report is the
   summary.
4. The lead (not the builder) merges and edits the shared files.

## Resume protocol

**A. One agent hit a usage limit.** After the reset, resume the same agent
by id with: "You were interrupted by a usage limit. Run
`git log --oneline origin/<base>..HEAD` and `git status`, then continue
from the first unfinished item. Commit and push as you go."

**B. The whole session ended (new session or account).**
1. `git fetch --all --prune`, `git worktree list`, and list open PRs.
2. For each branch in the roster, `git log --oneline origin/<base>..origin/<branch>`
   shows what is done and `git diff origin/<base>...origin/<branch> --stat`
   shows its footprint.
3. Launch a fresh builder per unfinished branch: "Check out
   `origin/<branch>`. The commits on it are finished; do not redo them.
   Read the spec and continue from the first unfinished item. Commit and
   push as you go."
4. Read the project's progress note and the latest collaborator-log entry,
   then run the setup verification script.

**C. A read-only agent (reviewer, QA) was cut off.** It left no commits.
Re-run it with the same brief; check `git branch -a` for review branches
it may have pushed; clean up any test data it created (by its tag).

## Roster ({{DATE}})

| Agent | Role / model class | Branch | State | Resume note |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| {{AGENT_ID}} | {{ROLE_AND_CLASS}} | {{BRANCH}} | {{running / finished / merged / cut off}} | {{NOTE}} |

Branch naming is the project's choice. If a rebase makes a plain push
fail, push a new branch name (for example a `-v2` suffix); never force-push.

